        }
      ],
      "verification": "Placeholder school scale, not a published grade boundary. Ofqual sets GCSE grade boundaries for each subject and each exam series after the papers are marked, so no fixed percentage-to-grade table exists and this pack must not claim one. The ten-point ladder is a school default for mocks and internal tests; grading_scales.gcse_9_1.bands is declared overridable so a school replaces it with the board's boundaries for the session. The points are the DfE 9-1 points used in Attainment 8 (grade 9 is 9 points, grade 1 is 1 point, U is 0), which are fixed national values."
    },
